    "biography": {
      "concept": "Game-show host of the silent marsh on the Odaroloc River (Act 6)",
      "notes": "Gloomgill hosts a quiz show in a silent marsh on the Odaroloc River, and he is also, somehow, the marsh. He wears a sequined game-show jacket over scales and holds a microphone that should not work under water and does. He is bright, pedantic and delighted, and he grades energy, not answers ('No pressure!'). There are no eliminations today, just consequences. He turns up where people are confident and wrong, and the marsh applauds."
    }
